    <!-- Logic -->
    <script>
        lucide.createIcons();

        const slides = document.querySelectorAll('.slide');
        const progressBar = document.getElementById('progress-bar');
        const notesModal = document.getElementById('notes-modal');
        const notesBackdrop = document.getElementById('notes-backdrop');
        const notesContent = document.getElementById('notes-content');
        const currentNoteDisplay = document.getElementById('current-note');
        
        let currentSlide = 0;
        let notesVisible = false;

        // The Deep Masterclass Coaching Script - Simplified and Culturally Grounded (11 slides total)
        const speakerNotes = [
            "Welcome, everyone. Today we are talking about YOU. In Africa, business has always been about community. We buy from the local vendor we know by name, not from a faceless building. Your personal brand is just taking that local trust and putting it online. By the end of this session, you will know exactly how to step out, build trust, and turn your good name into a solid business.",
            
            "Let's look at how things have changed. The old corporate way of hiding behind a slick logo does not work anymore. Africans buy from people they know and trust. We want to see the face behind the business. When people trust you—the founder—they automatically trust what you are selling. Your face and your honesty are your best marketing tools.",
            
            "Before we write a single post, we must build your foundation. Think of this as your brand blueprint. First, Vision: What is your big goal? Second, Values: What do you stand for? Think of 'Ubuntu'—I am because we are. Third, Voice: How do you speak? Keep it natural, like you are talking to a friend. Lastly, Visuals: Pick a consistent look and feel so people always recognize your work.",
            
            "Here is the truth: If you just call yourself a 'Consultant' or 'Marketer,' you are competing with thousands of others. You must stand out. Combine your unique African background, your struggles, and your professional skills. When you mix them together, you become the ONLY person who does what you do. You attract the right clients and naturally push away the bad ones.",
            
            "Now, where do you build this brand? Social media like X, TikTok, or LinkedIn is just a stage. You don't own it—they can delete your account tomorrow. You use social media to meet strangers. But the real goal is to move them into your 'Castle'—your own website or a private WhatsApp list. WhatsApp is where real African business and community happens. You must own your contacts.",
            
            "So, what do you actually post? Keep it simple: Educate, Connect, Promote. Spend 60% of your time teaching people things for free to show you are smart. Spend 30% sharing your human side, your struggles, and your real life to build trust. And spend 10% actually asking for the sale. Don't be afraid to tell people how to pay you. If you don't ask, you don't eat.",
            
            "As a Mental Health Advocate, I must stress this: Looking successful online comes with a heavy price. It brings endless DMs, pressure, and the reality of 'Black Tax' from extended family and friends. You must protect your peace. Decide today what parts of your life are totally private. Guard your energy, because a burned-out founder cannot run a business.",
            
            "We have a deep respect for the 'hustle'. People don't want to see a fake, polished, perfect life online—they know it's a lie. They want to see the real work. Show your messy desk. Talk about the deal you lost. When you are honest about your struggles and your hustle, people respect you more and they will support your journey.",
            
            "Once people trust you, how do you make money? You can sell digital guides and have people pay you instantly via Mobile Money like M-Pesa. As you grow, you can host group classes to reach more people at once. Eventually, big companies will pay you premium rates just to come speak on their stage or give them expert advice. Your brain becomes the product.",
            
            "This is the most important rule today: Building a brand is not a 'wash-wash' get-rich-quick scheme. It is a 10-year game to build generational wealth. Create content that will still be useful years from now. Use AI as a helpful assistant, but never lose your true voice. And never, ever sell your trust for quick money today. Your reputation is everything.",
            
            "We have covered your brand foundation, how to post, protecting your mental health, and how to make money from your knowledge. You have the blueprint. The only thing left is to start. So, I am opening the floor to you: What is the biggest thing holding you back from starting your personal brand today? Let's talk."
        ];

        function updateSlides() {
            slides.forEach((slide, index) => {
                slide.classList.remove('active', 'prev', 'next');
                if (index === currentSlide) {
                    slide.classList.add('active');
                } else if (index < currentSlide) {
                    slide.classList.add('prev');
                } else {
                    slide.classList.add('next');
                }
            });

            // Smooth Progress bar update
            const progress = ((currentSlide) / (slides.length - 1)) * 100;
            progressBar.style.width = `${progress}%`;

            // Update Notes with elegant typography
            currentNoteDisplay.innerHTML = `
                <div class="mb-6 flex items-center gap-3">
                    <span class="bg-brand-gold text-brand-blue font-bold px-3 py-1 rounded-lg text-sm tracking-widest uppercase">Slide ${currentSlide + 1}</span>
                </div>
                <p class="text-[1.35rem] text-gray-600 leading-relaxed">${speakerNotes[currentSlide]}</p>
            `;
        }

        function nextSlide() {
            if (currentSlide < slides.length - 1) {
                currentSlide++;
                updateSlides();
            }
        }

        function prevSlide() {
            if (currentSlide > 0) {
                currentSlide--;
                updateSlides();
            }
        }

        function toggleNotes() {
            notesVisible = !notesVisible;
            if (notesVisible) {
                notesModal.classList.remove('hidden');
                // Tiny delay to allow display:block to apply before animating opacity/transform
                setTimeout(() => {
                    notesBackdrop.classList.remove('opacity-0');
                    notesContent.classList.remove('translate-y-full');
                }, 20);
            } else {
                notesBackdrop.classList.add('opacity-0');
                notesContent.classList.add('translate-y-full');
                setTimeout(() => {
                    notesModal.classList.add('hidden');
                }, 500); // Wait for transition
            }
        }

        // Keyboard navigation
        document.addEventListener('keydown', (e) => {
            if (e.key === 'ArrowRight' || e.key === ' ') {
                nextSlide();
            } else if (e.key === 'ArrowLeft') {
                prevSlide();
            } else if (e.key === 'n' || e.key === 'N') {
                toggleNotes();
            }
        });

        // Swipe support for touch devices
        let touchStartX = 0;
        let touchEndX = 0;
        
        document.addEventListener('touchstart', e => {
            touchStartX = e.changedTouches[0].screenX;
        });

        document.addEventListener('touchend', e => {
            touchEndX = e.changedTouches[0].screenX;
            handleSwipe();
        });

        function handleSwipe() {
            const threshold = 50;
            if (touchEndX < touchStartX - threshold) nextSlide(); // Swipe left
            if (touchEndX > touchStartX + threshold) prevSlide(); // Swipe right
        }

        // Initialize
        updateSlides();
    </script>
